# Line endings: the tree is LF, everywhere, whatever the checkout does.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf` on gives every file a
# `\r` that the committed blob does not have, and every commit shows whole files
# rewritten. `eol=lf` also overrides `core.autocrlf` for the working copy.
#
# Binaries are detected by content (a NUL byte) and left alone; the explicit
# list is only for the assets where a future one might not be.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mkv binary
*.mp4 binary

# Bit-for-bit test material: `servermock/segments` holds real Twitch segments.
# (`*.ts` is deliberately not listed above: those are TypeScript sources.)
servermock/segments/** -text
